module

public import WeilConjectures.CategoryTheory.GrothendieckAbelian.HasDerivedCategory
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.Small
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.ColimitsOfShape
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.Subcategory
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.HomologicalFunctor
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.Opposite.Pretriangulated
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Grp.Abelian

/-! # Solution sets on set-generated localizing subcategories

Source: Neeman, *On the derived category of sheaves on a manifold*, Theorem 0.2;
Krause, *Localization theory for triangulated categories*, 7.2.1 and the construction
in 5.1.1; Krause, *Derived categories, resolutions, and Brown representability*, 4.5.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-set-generated-derived-solution-set)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe v u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.Opposite

namespace CategoryTheory

/-- The elements of a product-preserving cohomological functor on a set-generated
localizing subcategory of a Grothendieck derived category have a small weakly
universal family. This asserts neither uniqueness nor a representing object.

Source: Neeman, *On the derived category of sheaves on a manifold*, Theorem 0.2;
Krause, *Localization theory for triangulated categories*, Theorems 7.2.1 and 5.1.1;
the cellular construction in Krause, *Derived categories, resolutions, and Brown
representability*, Section 4.5.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-set-generated-derived-solution-set)

Proof: the ambient derived category is well generated by Neeman 0.2. Choose small
representatives of P and a common uncountable regular cardinal alpha for which the
ambient category is well generated and all these representatives are alpha-compact.
Krause 7.2.1 constructs a small family of alpha-small perfect generators of their
localizing hull. The containment and minimality hypotheses identify this hull with Q.
For the solution-set part of Brown's construction, close the generators under all
integer shifts. Form the coproduct of their pairs (generator, H-element), with its
universal element. Iteratively attach cones of all generator maps killed by this
element, lifting the element by cohomological exactness at each stage. Take the
sequential telescope and lift the compatible elements using exactness on its defining
triangle and the product hypothesis. In the abelian category of coherent functors on the additive
closure of the perfect
family, perfectness identifies the restricted telescope with the colimit of stages.
The universal transformation is therefore bijective on the generators and shifts.
The class on which it is bijective is triangulated and closed under coproducts, so
minimality makes it all of Q. Retaining just surjectivity gives the asserted family
(one object suffices). Every stage and index set is in universe v: the perfect
family, Hom sets and H-values are v-small. No compactness of the original P is used.
-/
theorem setGeneratedDerived_cohomological_solutionSet
    {A : Type u} [Category.{v} A] [Abelian A]
    [IsGrothendieckAbelian.{v} A] [HasDerivedCategory.{v} A]
    (P Q : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory A))
    [ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.{v} P]
    [Q.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms] [Q.IsTriangulated]
    [∀ I : Type v, Q.IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape (Discrete I)]
    (hP : P ≤ Q)
    (hminimal : ∀ R : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory A), P ≤ R →
      R.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms → R.IsTriangulated →
      (∀ I : Type v, R.IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape (Discrete I)) → Q ≤ R)
    (H : Q.FullSubcategoryᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{v}) [H.IsHomological]
    (hH : ∀ I : Type v, PreservesLimitsOfShape (Discrete I) H) :
    ∃ (I : Type v) (B : I → Q.FullSubcategory) (b : ∀ i, H.obj (op (B i))),
      ∀ (Z : Q.FullSubcategory) (z : H.obj (op Z)), ∃ (i : I) (f : Z ⟶ B i),
        H.map f.op (b i) = z := by
  sorry

end CategoryTheory
